00:01:44.944 --> 00:01:49.245
The idea of the four horsemen originates from Christian myth.

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:51.884
They appear in three main books.

00:01:51.884 --> 00:01:58.397
In the old testament the riders can be found in the book of Zechariah and the book of Ezekiel.

00:01:58.397 --> 00:02:03.634
In the new testament John of Patmos talks about them in the book of revelation.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:12.816
Chapter 6 of revelation talks about a scroll in the right hand of God that has been sealed shut by seven individual seals.

00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:24.987
When the lamb of God opens the first four of these seven seals he shall summon forth four beings that ride on white, red, black and pale horses.

00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:33.324
Out of these four riders only death is named in the bible but the rest have been named by what they represent.

00:02:33.324 --> 00:02:38.622
The lamb of God for those unfamiliar is a title given to Jesus Christ.

00:02:38.622 --> 00:02:49.738
Which leads us to believe that if Jesus himself is opening these seals and unleashing the apocalypse upon humanity then maybe this has been ordained by God.

00:02:49.738 --> 00:02:55.960
Maybe it is a future or punishment humanity brought upon itself.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:04.550
The first horseman to appear is the rider in white, the horseman of conquest.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:27.718
“Then I saw when the Lamb broke one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures saying as with a voice of thunder, "Come." I looked, and behold, a white horse, and he who sat on it had a bow; and a crown was given to him, and he went out conquering and to conquer”

00:03:27.718 --> 00:03:31.838
This horseman has been interpreted in several different ways,

00:03:31.838 --> 00:03:36.764
In this context conquering meant spreading the word of god across the land.

00:03:36.764 --> 00:03:46.638
The reason this rider is dressed in white would have been because traditionally it’s a colour the bible associates with purity, christ and righteousness.

00:03:46.638 --> 00:03:57.151
In the mid 19th century there were some who claimed this horseman represented something closer to the Anti Christ and was not to be seen as a positive figure.

00:03:57.151 --> 00:04:05.615
The white horseman was also thought to symbolize war which would make sense considering war and conquest often go hand in hand.

00:04:05.615 --> 00:04:09.980
But war is more commonly associated with the red horseman.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:18.956
You may also see that many refer to the first horseman as pestilence instead of conquest and there are few reasons for this.

00:04:18.956 --> 00:04:21.738
War and conquest are quite similar

00:04:21.738 --> 00:04:32.598
and so in the last few hundred years writers and scholars have instead associated the first horseman with infectious disease, the bringer of plague.

00:04:33.046 --> 00:04:37.527
The Romans interpreted all four horsemen slightly differently,

00:04:37.527 --> 00:04:43.361
they saw them as representing or prophesying the future of the Roman empire.

00:04:43.361 --> 00:04:49.794
The colour white to them was symbolic of triumph, political success and prosperity.

00:04:49.794 --> 00:04:58.371
Although the white horseman may not be seen as christ or religion by the Romans they also some him largely as a positive figure.

00:04:59.034 --> 00:05:04.946
The second Horseman is the rider in red, the horseman of war.

00:05:04.946 --> 00:05:25.685
“When He broke the second seal, I heard the second living creature saying, "Come." And another, a red horse, went out; and to him who sat on it, it was granted to take peace from Earth, and that men would slay one another; and a great sword was given to him.”

00:05:25.685 --> 00:05:36.523
Everything about the second horseman is fairly straightforward; he rides on a fiery red horse with his greatsword held upwards as a declaration of war.

00:05:36.523 --> 00:05:47.041
Upwards facing swords would often signify the intention to enter battle and the colour red we can assume symbolises the bloodshed that comes with war.

00:05:47.041 --> 00:05:53.528
The white and red horseman were both connected to war but not the same type.

00:05:53.528 --> 00:05:58.662
Conquest implies trying to seize control of something through military force.

00:05:58.662 --> 00:06:05.752
In the case of the Horseman of conquest that would mean spreading the word of god to those who may be of a different or no faith.

00:06:05.752 --> 00:06:11.439
“It was granted to take peace from earth and that men would say one another”

00:06:11.439 --> 00:06:17.623
it's this passage that led scholars to interpret the horsemen of war as representing civil war.

00:06:17.623 --> 00:06:26.419
If we go back to the Romans empire, the white horseman was symbolic of the success of Rome, the red horseman however not so much.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:35.609
The second seal being broken meant peace left Rome, there was bloodshed, civil war and insurrection in the empire.

00:06:35.609 --> 00:06:47.167
This is attributed to the Roman emperor Commodus whose reign is considered to mark the end of the golden era within Rome and the beginning of civil unrest.

00:06:49.132 --> 00:06:54.426
The third horseman is the black rider, the horseman of famine.

00:06:54.426 --> 00:07:24.099
When He broke the third seal, I heard the third living creature saying, "Come." I looked, and behold, a black horse; and he who sat on it had a pair of scales in his hand. And I heard something like a voice in the center of the four living creatures saying, "A quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius; but do not damage the oil and the wine."

00:07:24.726 --> 00:07:30.919
Some believe the scales the horseman holds can be interpreted as the scales of justice,

00:07:30.919 --> 00:07:36.784
others believe the scales actually reflect how bread used to be weighed in times of famine.

00:07:36.784 --> 00:07:43.332
The mention of barley and wheat in the above passage is why the later interpretation is used more commonly.

00:07:43.332 --> 00:07:54.052
The prices mentioned may not make much sense now but it roughly translates to an entire day's work just to buy some of the ingredients to make bread

00:07:54.052 --> 00:07:57.310
so you can see why they may have caused a famine.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:02.352
It also mentions the price of oil and wine remains untouched

00:08:02.352 --> 00:08:06.585
but these were luxuries way out of the price range of a common worker.

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:17.257
This can be taken in a literal sense as a plague of locusts could easily ravage crops but grapevines and olive branches were a bit more resolute.

00:08:17.257 --> 00:08:28.909
If the horseman is bringing this famine as punishment then going after the necessities such as wheat and barley which offer little resistance but are of grave importance makes sense.

00:08:28.909 --> 00:08:40.665
If we once again go back to the Roman empire, the third horseman and the increasing costs of basic necessities would represent the excessive taxation of Roman citizens.

00:08:40.665 --> 00:08:48.987
That led to the rich continuing their lavish lifestyles whilst everyone else struggled just to feed their families.

00:08:50.736 --> 00:08:54.885
The fourth and final horseman is the pale rider,

00:08:54.885 --> 00:09:02.200
many scholars describe a sickly appearance as opposed to a specific colour like the other horseman

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:10.650
in later artistic interpretations the colour green is what we associate with the horseman of death.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:39.375
When the Lamb broke the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature saying, "Come." I looked, and behold, a pale horse; and he who sat on it had the name Death; and Hades was following with him. Authority was given to them over a fourth of the earth, to kill with sword and with famine and with pestilence and by the wild beasts of the earth.”

00:09:39.375 --> 00:09:43.809
The fourth horseman is the only one to be named,

00:09:43.809 --> 00:09:52.677
he is also referred to as Thanatos, a greek deity or spirit associated with non violent death.

00:09:52.677 --> 00:09:57.313
Death is also described as being followed by Hades

00:09:57.313 --> 00:10:04.774
which in this sense may not necessarily mean the god himself but more so Hades the resting place of the dead.

00:10:04.774 --> 00:10:16.084
"Authority was given to them over a fourth of the earth, to kill with sword and with famine and with pestilence and by the wild beasts of the earth.”

00:10:16.084 --> 00:10:23.308
This can be interpreted as Death being given authority to kill and Hades to take these souls

00:10:23.308 --> 00:10:31.619
but the fact it mentions by sword, famine, and pestilence you would imagine this passage refers to all four horsemen.

00:10:31.619 --> 00:10:39.467
After years of carnage, famine, oppression and failures by the empire to look after it’s people

00:10:39.467 --> 00:10:44.220
death would mark the dissolution of the Roman empire.

00:10:44.668 --> 00:10:49.060
The four horsemen have been interpreted in many different ways,

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:58.276
one being as a prophecy of the great tribulation. A series of judgments from God that caused many on earth to die,

00:10:58.276 --> 00:11:06.365
those who repented for their sins and accepted him as their savior would form a new world with those who remained faithful.

00:11:06.365 --> 00:11:10.200
The horsemen were the first of these many judgments,

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:15.402
the first seal being broken signifying the arrival of the antichrist,

00:11:15.402 --> 00:11:17.805
the second was global war,

00:11:17.805 --> 00:11:20.542
the third economic collapse

00:11:20.542 --> 00:11:24.904
and the last the death of a ¼ of the world population.

00:11:24.904 --> 00:11:29.659
The book of Zechariah takes a different approach to the four horsemen.

00:11:29.659 --> 00:11:38.106
Here they are known as four spirits who descend from heaven on chariots each with a different coloured horse.

00:11:38.106 --> 00:11:43.116
Unlike in revelation their role here is not to bring the apolcaplyse,

00:11:43.116 --> 00:11:47.435
they were sent to patrol the earth and maintain peace

00:11:47.435 --> 00:11:53.626
so the account in Zechariah is pretty much the opposite to revelation.

00:11:53.626 --> 00:11:56.394
Hopefully this has shed some light of the four horsemen.

00:11:56.394 --> 00:12:03.116
 If you like to share some of your favourite references of the four horseman then feel free to do so in the comment section.

